# Loading-State Validation

Lazy panels show a Suspense fallback while their chunk loads. Local chunks load fast — add a temp 2s delay to the `lazy()` import (or CPU-throttle in DevTools) to actually see each fallback.

## Suspense fallbacks (skeletons)

| # | State | How to trigger | Fallback | Expected look | Pass criteria |
|---|-------|----------------|----------|---------------|---------------|
| 1 | BrowserPanel | Fresh task → toggle Browser panel | `PanelLoadingSkeleton` | Header bar (title pill + 2 icon btns) over 4 staggered content lines, inside panel chrome (bg-surface-1, border, rounded) | Skeleton fills panel exactly, no blank flash, no size jump when real panel swaps in |
| 2 | FileEditorView | Toggle Editor panel (repo task) | `PanelLoadingSkeleton` | same | same |
| 3 | UnifiedGitPanel | Toggle Git/Diff panel | `PanelLoadingSkeleton` | same | same |
| 4 | ArtifactsPanel | Toggle Artifacts panel | `PanelLoadingSkeleton` | same | same |
| 5 | ChatPanel | Open chat-mode terminal tab (claude-chat / codex-chat) | `ChatPanelSkeleton` | Empty body + bottom input-bar skeleton (h-9, full width) pinned to bottom | Bottom bar aligns w/ real composer, no top-header skeleton |
| 6 | TreeView | Switch sidebar to Tree view | `animate-pulse bg-sidebar` | Full sidebar area pulses in sidebar color | Pulse fills sidebar width, no white flash |
| 7 | TaskDetailPage (secondary window) | Open task in secondary window | `TaskShell` | Full task-layout skeleton (header + body) | Matches main task layout shape |

## Null fallbacks (validate: NO flash / NO layout shift)

| # | State | Trigger | Fallback | Pass criteria |
|---|-------|---------|----------|---------------|
| 8 | KanbanBoard | Home tab, board view | `null` | No flicker; board appears cleanly |
| 9 | KanbanListView | Home tab, list view | `null` | same |
| 10 | FilterBar | Project w/ tasks | `null` | No gap/jump in toolbar |
| 11 | GlobalAgentSidePanel | Open global agent panel | `null` | Wrapper chrome holds width; content fills in |
| 12 | AgentStatusSidePanel | Lock agent-status panel | `null` | No flash |
| 13 | RichTextEditor (inline desc) | Open task w/ description | `<div h-20>` | No layout jump; spacer matches editor min-height |
| 14 | DescriptionDialog | Open description fullscreen | `null` | Dialog opens once loaded, no half-render |

## CSS animations (framer removed — validate motion still feels right)

| # | State | Trigger | Mechanism | Pass criteria |
|---|-------|---------|-----------|---------------|
| 15 | Button tap | Press any Button | CSS `active:scale-[0.98]` | Quick press-shrink, springs back, disabled btns inert |
| 16 | UpdateToast in/out | Update ready → dismiss | `usePresence` + tw-animate-css | Slides up+fades in from bottom; slides down+fades out on dismiss; text stays during exit |
| 17 | DevServerToast in/out | Dev server detected → dismiss | same | same (bottom-center) |

## Test recipe
1. Add temp delay to a `lazy()` import: `new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 2000)).then(() => import(...))`
2. `pnpm dev`
3. Trigger each row above, screenshot the fallback
4. Confirm pass criteria (fill, no flash, no shift)
5. Revert temp delays
